      {
        "id": 176136,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-06-01T02:12:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Entering a hazard space triggers an attack. &nbsp;That part was definitely correct. &nbsp;Spawning a target involves that target entering the hex they spawn in.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I agree that the order of application of Shared Burden vs. Regression Burst whould have been decided by the active player. &nbsp;The wording on the card reduces the damage to 1 and then places a new Proletariat.</p><p><span>Both Shared Burden and Regression react to damage dealt, which means they will both try to act immediately after health is removed.<br>For the effect to cut in line ahead of Regression Burst the placing of the clone would have to be before proletariat took the damage.</span></p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:59:51.198Z",
