        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Entering a hazard space triggers an attack. &nbsp;That part was definitely correct. &nbsp;Spawning a target involves that target entering the hex they spawn in.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I agree that the order of application of Shared Burden vs. Regression Burst whould have been decided by the active player. &nbsp;The wording on the card reduces the damage to 1 and then places a new Proletariat.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Both Shared Burden and Regression react to damage dealt, which means they will both try to act immediately after health is removed.<br />For the effect to cut in line ahead of Regression Burst the placing of the clone would have to be before proletariat took the damage.</span></p><p><br />&nbsp;</p>",
